!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The Toronto KnockOut (TKO) CRISPR Library - Version 1 (90K sub-library) was used (addgene catalog# 1000000069). Protocol of library construction is detailed in Hart et al. High-Resolution CRISPR Screens Reveal Fitness Genes and Genotype-Specific Cancer Liabilities. Cell. 2015;163(6):1515-26.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Pooled genome-wide CRISPR/Ca9 knockout screen
!Sample_description = DMSO, day 36, replicate#1
!Sample_description = IC0 T36_A
!Sample_data_processing = Basecalls performed using Illumina RTA version 2.4.11
!Sample_data_processing = Reads in fastq files are trimmed then mapped to the sgRNA library using bowtie
!Sample_data_processing = A python script uses samtools to count the mapped reads in the bam files and report the raw counts
!Sample_data_processing = Raw mapped counts were used as input to MaGECK algorithm to rank top hits
!Sample_data_processing = To normalize the raw counts, read counts for each sgRNA was divided by the total sum of read counts for that sample, and multiplied by 1,000,000 to give a count per million mapped reads for each sgRNA. To convert to log 2, 1 was added to each sample, followed by taking log2
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Text file with genes and their targeting sgRNAs including the sequences and counts (raw, normalized and log2 normalized) of these sgRNAs across all sample replicates
!Sample_platform_id = GPL18573
