^SAMPLE = GSM5015827
!Sample_title = IC0 T36_B
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM5015827
!Sample_status = Public on Jan 13 2021
!Sample_submission_date = Jan 12 2021
!Sample_last_update_date = Jan 13 2021
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = OCI-AML2 cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tumor: Acute myeloid leukemia
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = agent: DMSO
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = time point: day 36
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Myeloid blood cells
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Cells were treated with DMSO or TAK-243 at its IC90 (25 nM) or IC99 (30 nM) for 32 days or 36 days
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = OCI-AML2 were cultured in Iscove’s modified Dulbecco’s medium (IMDM). The genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 knockout screen was performed in OCI-AML2 cells stably expressing Cas9 (OCI-AML2-Cas9). To generate these cells, OCI-AML2 cells were transduced with a Cas9 in a lentiviral vector, Lenti-Cas9-2A-Blast (Addgene plasmid#73310). The cells were selected with blasticidin (10 μg/mL) for 6 days. Single-cell clones were obtained by plating in a 96-well plate at a density of 0.4 cell/well, and a clonal population with high Cas9 expression was selected.  OCI-AML2-Cas9 cells were transduced with a pooled library (TKO-90k library) of 91,320 guide RNAs (gRNAs) in lentiviral vectors targeting 17,232 genes at a ratio of 6 gRNAs per gene. These cells were transduced at a multiplicity of infection (MOI) of approximately 0.3-0.4 to obtain coverage of at least 200-fold per gRNA. One day post-transduction, cells were treated with puromycin (2μg/mL) for 48h to select transduced cells.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was extracted from pellets of 20-50x10^6 cells using the QIAamp Blood Maxi kit (Cat#51194)
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The Toronto KnockOut (TKO) CRISPR Library - Version 1 (90K sub-library) was used (addgene catalog# 1000000069). Protocol of library construction is detailed in Hart et al. High-Resolution CRISPR Screens Reveal Fitness Genes and Genotype-Specific Cancer Liabilities. Cell. 2015;163(6):1515-26.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Pooled genome-wide CRISPR/Ca9 knockout screen
